From: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android-gadget-start: retry UDC bind until FunctionFS is ready

adbd (started as the unit's ExecStart) must open the FunctionFS control
endpoint and write its descriptors/strings before the composite gadget
can be bound to the UDC. android-gadget-start runs as ExecStartPost and
races adbd: if it writes the UDC name before adbd has populated the
FunctionFS descriptors (ep1/ep2), the kernel rejects the bind with
-ENODEV:

    udc a600000.usb: failed to start adb: -19
    UDC core: adb: couldn't find an available UDC or it's busy

Because the script runs under 'set -e', that single failed write aborts
the script, fails the unit, and android-tools-adbd.service ends up in a
restart loop ("Start request repeated too quickly").

Retry the UDC write until it succeeds (up to ~30s) instead of giving up
on the first attempt. Once adbd has written its descriptors the bind
succeeds and the gadget enumerates normally.

Observed on IMDT QCS8550 SBC (dwc3-qcom, UDC a600000.usb).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
---
 android-gadget-start | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/android-gadget-start
+++ b/android-gadget-start
@@ -104,4 +104,13 @@
 fi

 echo "Binding Gadget to UDC: $best_udc (maximum_speed='$(read_max_speed "$UDC_FOLDER/$best_udc")')" >&2
-echo -n "$best_udc" > "$GADGET_PATH/UDC"
+n=0
+while ! echo -n "$best_udc" > "$GADGET_PATH/UDC" 2>/dev/null; do
+    n=$((n + 1))
+    if [ "$n" -ge 30 ]; then
+        echo "Error: timed out binding UDC $best_udc after ${n} attempts" >&2
+        exit 1
+    fi
+    sleep 1
+done
+echo "Bound UDC $best_udc after $n attempt(s)" >&2
